```plaintext
2result.sql
```


**Why**

2result.sql  
• Labels each page_view as PLP or PDP with clear category + “+” rules.  
• For every individual PLP view it looks for a *later* PDP inside the same
  (user + ga_session_id) session, so a PLP is counted as a transition only when it is
  truly followed by a PDP.  
• This fulfils “eventually led to a PDP in the same session” exactly.  

0result.sql inflates the numerator by counting *all* PLPs that sit in any session
where at least one PLP happens before the first PDP (so PLPs after the PDP are
also counted).  
1result.sql does the opposite: it discards PLPs that occur after the first PDP,
thus under‑counting valid transitions when several PDPs exist later in the
session.

Hence 2result.sql gives the most accurate answer.